.TH SCANDOR 1 "Saphira Candor" "Saphira Candor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scandor \- Self-Contained Candor; the Candor engine sealed into one executable
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scandor --context
.I T
.RB [ --question
.IR T ]
.B --candidate
.I A
.RB [ --candidate
.IR B ...]
.RB [ --head
.IR forward|inverse|both ]
.RB [ --json ]
.br
.B scandor --help | --version | --about
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBscandor\fR is Candor with its model and witnessed facts compiled into the
executable itself. It opens no model file, no data file, no witness file:
copy the binary anywhere -- an empty directory, a floppy -- and it answers
identically. Same engine and same verdict discipline as \fBcandor\fR(1);
the only difference is where the bytes come from.
.SH VERDICTS
Every answer carries exactly one verdict:
.TP
.B REMEMBERED
Exactly one candidate matches a baked witnessed (entity, property) fact. The
source statement is printed and the neural forward pass is skipped entirely.
.TP
.B GUESSED
No baked fact answered. The compiled-in forward pass runs and its
scores/probabilities are reported, marked as a guess. A guess is never
presented as a memory.
.PP
Absence is never a denial: an unwitnessed candidate is reported as not in
memory, never as false.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --context " T" ", " --question " T"
Question text. The entity is resolved from the context against baked witnesses.
.TP
.BR --candidate " A"
One answer option; repeatable, up to 64.
.TP
.BR --head " forward|inverse|both"
Which judgement head answers (default forward).
.TP
.B --json
Machine-readable output: \fB{"verdict": "remembered"|"guessed", ...}\fR.
.TP
.BR --version ", " --about
\fB--version\fR prints the product version. \fB--about\fR prints the baked
provenance: model and witness sha256, row counts, container version --
auditing any binary back to its exact training.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Answered (either verdict).
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure (embedded content unreadable: a build defect, never user data).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
scandor --context "What is true of the tract0007 pipit?" \\
  --candidate alert --candidate louder
scandor --about
.fi
.SH FILES
None. This binary reads no files at runtime.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR candor (1)
